      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kael Drakkel, The King's Madness [zone=869]\n**Who:**\n- Captain Bvellos [npc=41305]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Faction Required:**\nDragon Death Keep (Min: Indifferent)\n**Quest Items:**\n- Fearforged Dagger [item=106625]\n- Large Sliver of Fear [item=106915]\n- Note from Svekk [item=106632]\n- Small Sliver of Fear [item=108829]\n**Related Zones:**\n- East Wastes, Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening [zone=868]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Drjek [npc=41570]\n- Svekk Fangbinder [npc=41961]\n- Wevek Redforge [npc=42091]\n- a coldain marauder [npc=41528]\n- a courier [npc=41662]\n- a hostile apparition [npc=42111]\n- a smuggler - East Wastes - RoF [npc=41549]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Kael #2: Them Bones [quest=6060]\n- Kael #3: A Cure for Madness [quest=6061]\n- Raid Expedition: The Madness of King Tormax [quest=6064]\n- The Madness of King Tormax [quest=6063]\n- Traitors Among Us [quest=6062]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 21:25:15 2012\nModified: Sun Nov 9 13:10:25 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis is the first task in a series of three. It is a solo task that begins with Captain Bvellos [npc=41305] ( map) in the bank of Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness. He is found inside the bank at /location -300, 1420, -195 (the bank is in the center of the city).\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Must have at least indifferent faction with Dragon Death Keep (kill frost giants and/or apparitions to increase it)\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Bvellos'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'Halt! As a captain commissioned by the authority of King Tormax, I ought to remove you from the city immediately, or kill you where you stand. You have heard his orders have you not? All mercenaries have henceforth been barred from entering Kael Drakkel. But we both know decrees pronounced in citadels are rarely heard or regarded in alleyways. I have seen your kind skulking in dark corners -- I have [seen] many things as of late.'\nYou say, 'What have you seen?'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'Mercenaries coming and going, couriers rushing about, concealing heavy bundles. Strange apparitions appearing -- just last night I stabbed my father through the heart as he tried to tear off my skin with his teeth. And he has been dead for twenty years. No sooner had I plunged my dagger into him than he disappeared into the night like a mist. Nothing has seemed real since we received these new [weapons] from Tormax's court.'\nYou say, 'What weapons?'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'These blades, glowing with power -- surely they have some connection with the madness that has gripped the king and suffused the city. Shortly after the kromzek received these new weapons, King Tormax made his mad decrees. Mercenaries were expelled from the city, living visions began to haunt the citizenry, coldain and dragons made incursions into the city, and the kromzek were ordered to regard the kromrif with suspicion, watching them for evidence of their hand in the strange events. Now I have seen [couriers] rushing throughout the city. Wherever they stop, more apparitions and unrest appear.'\nYou say, 'Couriers?'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'I have my suspicions about who they are working for, but I need proof. I cannot easily raise my hand against them lest it draw outrage from the king. As much as I dislike it, I need mercenaries such as you. If you are [willing], waylay any couriers you see, and bring what they are carrying. If I can trace the origin of these new weapons, perhaps I can put an end to the madness that has descended upon Kael.'\nYou say, 'I am willing'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'Hurry. I do not want to meet my father again in this life.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Deliver Us Unto Evil'.\nCaptain Bvellos believes the new weapons given to the giants of Kael are somehow the cause of the chaos in the city. He has asked you to track down the source of the weapons.\nKill the couriers wandering throughout Kael and find any evidence they are carrying.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Steal the goods that the couriers in Kael are carrying 0/4 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nLoot 4 Fearforged Daggers [item=106625] from a courier [npc=41662] that wanders the zone (note: the couriers do not have faction hits).\n2\\. Find evidence on the couriers that reveals their distribution source 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nKill another courier and loot a Note From Svekk [item=106632].\n3\\. Deliver the stolen weapons to Captain Bvellos 0/4 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nCaptain Bvellos says 'These are the weapons you recovered from the couriers? Then it is as I thought. The weapons are still being distributed throughout the city. If you have any further evidence of who commands the couriers, let me see it.'\n4\\. Show Captain Bvellos the note from Svekk 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nCaptain Bvellos says 'Svekk Fangbinder, Wenglawks's lackey -- I should have guessed. Did you read this note? Apparently Svekk has been hiring mercenaries to smuggle materials into Kael, which are then used to forge the new weapons. Being a mercenary yourself, perhaps you could offer your services to Svekk. Convince him to send you on a smuggling run. Discover where the materials are coming from, and where they are delivered. Once I know, I can move against Svekk. Kael will yet be returned to its equilibrium!'\n\n---\n\n5\\. Ask Svekk Fangbinder if you can work for him 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ According to the note you found on a courier, Svekk Fangbinder has been coordinating shipments of material entering the city and the forging of weapons. Captain Bvellos suggests you offer your services to Svekk as a smuggler, so you can discover more about the operation.\nSvekk Fangbinder [npc=41961] ( map) is at /location 155, 1950, -191 (in a building in the northwestern part of the city's center - this is northwest of the bank).\nYou say, 'Hail, Svekk Fangbinder'\nSvekk Fangbinder says 'What? You wish to deliver goods for me? It's certainly bold of you to stride around Kael in daylight when the king's threat hangs over your head. I can use someone like you. I want you to have a talk with my contact in the Eastern Wastes, Drjek. He has a delivery that needs to enter Kael unnoticed.'\n6\\. Tell Drjek that Svekk has sent you 0/1 (Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening)\n_Task Window Says:_ You have been hired as a smuggler, working for Svekk Fangbinder. Drjek in Eastern Wastes has a shipment for you to pick up.\nDrjek [npc=41570] ( map) is found in the northwestern part of Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening at around -4380, 4045, 143 (about halfway between Kael and the giant fort).\nYou say, 'Hail, Drjek'\nDrjek says 'Delivery? I do not have time to worry about such things with these greedy coldain marauders attacking our operation. Take care of them, and then we can talk!'\n7\\. Kill 3 coldain marauders 0/3 (Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening)\n_Task Window Says:_ Coldain marauders are attacking Drjek's outpost. You must defeat them before you can pick up the shipment.\nKill the Coldain marauders fighting the orcs next to Drjek.\n8\\. Hail Drjek and receive the shipment 0/1 (Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening)\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that it is safe, tell Drjek you are ready to transport the shipment.\nYou say, 'Hail, Drjek'\nDrjek says 'Well, you look a whit healthier than the last whelps Svekk sent me, and you did handle those coldain admirably. This is the largest sliver of crystal I have yet acquired. Deliver it to Wevek Redforge -- he is waiting for it to forge another set of weapons for the kromzek. Oh, and if you see any of my other delivery agents on your way, go ahead and kill them. Finish their deliveries for them. I know they are stealing from us! I think you are the only one I can trust! But If I find out otherwise...I might have to deliver everything myself.'\nYou receive Large Sliver of Fear [item=106915].\n\n---\n\n9\\. (Optional) Steal small slivers of crystal from untrustworthy smugglers 0/4 (Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening)\n10\\. (Optional) Deliver the small slivers of crystal to Captain Bvellos 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n11\\. Head to Wevek Redforge and confront anything that impedes your progress 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n12\\. Kill 2 hostile apparitions 0/2 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ Drjek has told you to deliver a large crystal sliver to Wevek Redforge. Drjek also said he doesn't trust most of his smugglers. If you see any, kill them and deliver their goods to Captain Bvellos for examination. The large crystal you are carrying has the potential to generate nightmarish creatures. If this happens, kill the creatures.\nFor the optional steps, smugglers [npc=41549] can be found in the canyon leading to Kael Drakkel. Kill them until you have looted 4x Small Sliver of Fear [item=108829], then give those items to Bvellos.\nNote that the two hostile apparitions [npc=42111] will spawn on you at a random time after you re-enter Kael. You can just stay at the zone-in area and await their spawn or chance making your way through the city. They each hit for a max ~13,000; AE rampage; cast \"Crippling Contusion\"; and have about 2.7 million hitpoints each. They are known to be rootable and mezzable, and they do not summon.\nCrippling Contusion: Targeted AE 25', Magic (-940)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 27000\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 8000 per tick _(3 ticks)_\n3: Decrease Attack Speed by 50%\n4: Increase Curse Counter by 25\nWevek Redforge [npc=42091] ( map) is found at location 250, 850, -130. If coming from the Eastern Wastes, pass through the first archway, keep going, pass through the second archway, and hang an immediate right (north). He is in a building in the northeastern part of this area.\nUpon turning in the optional element:\nCaptain Bvellos says 'So this is what the mercenaries have been sneaking into Kael? By the power of Zek, what malevolence emanates from these crystals? I feel the world growing smaller and darker just holding one in my hand. If blades are being forged with this material, it is no surprise why insanity has descended upon Kael.'\nThe other steps update upon the deaths of the hostile apparitions.\n\n---\n\n13\\. Deliver the large crystal sliver to Wevek Redforge 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n14\\. Ask Wevek Redforge what he knows about the crystal deliveries 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wevek Redforge'\nWevek Redforge says 'Are you feeling alright? You look pale. Most mercenaries who bring me supplies arrive looking nervous and haggard. You are no exception. ' As Wevek takes the large crystal sliver from you, his gloved hands tremble, and his eyes reflect the purple light of the crystal. 'I hate these things. How much strife has rung throughout this city with every blow of my hammer against the anvil? But I cannot stop forging the weapons that will bring ruin upon my brethren. They will not let me...'\nWevek Redforge says 'No, do not make me say who it is that compels my work!'\nDrjek says 'Silence, Wevek! Not another word to these pack mules! Do you want Wenglawks to hear that your mouth has been more active than your hammer?' Drjek glowers at you. 'It looks like you did your job, but remember my words: Do what you are told and do not ask questions, unless you want to end your days in a block of ice.'\nWevek Redforge says 'Apologies, Drjek. My hammering will be the only sound you hear from me.'\n15\\. Tell Bvellos what you learned from Svekk Fangbinder 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ Drjek threatened Wevek Redforge, and in the process revealed that Wenglawks Kkeak is involved in creating the malevolent weapons. Inform Captain Bvellos of what you have learned.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Bvellos'\nCaptain Bvellos says 'Wenglawks has been coordinating the shipments of crystal and the forging of weapons? I have suspected he might be involved, but now I have proof. His treachery will not escape punishment much longer! You must relay this information to Rejnak Coldspear, Fjokar Frozenshard's retainer. He has been investigating some additional leads, and your discoveries will undoubtedly assist him. Perhaps soon I will be able to sleep without my sword at my side.'\nYou have discovered Wenglawks Kkeak has been coordinating deliveries of crystal shards and the forging of weapons. Speak with Fjokar Frozenshard's retainer, Rejnak Coldspear, and see if this information will aid his investigation.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience (3 AAs + 2-3% exp in Level 96)",
    },
