      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kael Drakkel, The King's Madness [zone=869]\n**Who:**\n- Rejnak Coldspear [npc=41306]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 85\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nDragon Death Keep\n**Quest Items:**\n- Barrier Breaker [item=106613]\n- Crystal Remains [item=106593]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Kael Drakkel: Traitors Among Us [zone=886]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Bjoskhua Blackfist [npc=42579]\n- Captain Bvellos [npc=42587]\n- Clrakk Blackfist [npc=42580]\n- Fjokar Frozenshard [npc=42586]\n- Gkrean Prophet of Tallon [npc=42598]\n- King Tormax [npc=42594]\n- Klaggan Iceshard [npc=42582]\n- Kyenka - RoF - 2 [npc=42595]\n- Noble Helssen [npc=42584]\n- Nojas Blackfist [npc=42581]\n- Rejnak Coldspear [npc=42585]\n- Semkak Prophet of Vallon [npc=42597]\n- Vorken Iceshard [npc=42583]\n- Wenglawks Kkeak - RoF - 2 [npc=42600]\n- Wevek Redforge [npc=42481]\n- Yetarr [npc=42596]\n- a chest - Traitors Among Us [npc=42446]\n- a crystal guard [npc=42591]\n- a crystal of fear [npc=42599]\n- a crystal shard [npc=42592]\n- a shard seeker [npc=42593]\n- an ice wall [npc=42588]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Kael #1: Deliver Us Unto Evil [quest=6059]\n- Kael #2: Them Bones [quest=6060]\n- Kael #3: A Cure for Madness [quest=6061]\n- Raid Expedition: The Madness of King Tormax [quest=6064]\n- The Madness of King Tormax [quest=6063]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 21:25:27 2012\nModified: Sun Nov 9 18:50:14 2025 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis is a group mission that begins with Rejnak Coldspear [npc=41306] ( map) in Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness. He is located behind the throne room of the zone (southernmost point in the zone) - in the east back room.\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed Deliver Us Unto Evil [quest=6059]\n\\- Completed Them Bones [quest=6060]\n\\- Completed A Cure for Madness [quest=6061]\n\\- Must have positive faction with Dragon Death Keep (kill frost giants and/or apparitions to increase it)\nYou say, 'Hail, Rejnak Coldspear'\nRejnak Coldspear says 'You have done well collecting [evidence]! I don't like what has been discovered, though...'\nRejnak Coldspear says 'The truth is painful, but our response will be more so: The Iceshard brothers have betrayed the King and every citizen of Kael. You have proven this to us, and now we must act. Fjokar and Noble Helssen are readying to meet Captain Bvellos and [assault] Iceshard Manor. Though once they were our brethren, Klaggan and Vorken will not live beyond this day.'\nYou say, 'An assault?'\nRejnak Coldspear says 'If you wish to assist, [meet] us outside Dragondeath Keep. The Iceshards shall rue the day they brought madness upon Kael!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Traitors Among Us'.\nWith your help, Captain Bvellos and Noble Helssen have determined the Iceshard brothers are responsible for causing the King's malady and bringing chaos to Kael. Now you must join the attack upon Iceshard Manor to punish the traitors.\nYou say, 'I'll meet you there!'\nRejnak Coldspear says 'I shall see you soon, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Kael Drakkel Mission.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Speak with Noble Helssen 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou'll have a few giants assisting you through this mission. They will follow you automatically.\nYou say, 'Hail, Noble Helssen'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Captain Bvellos waits outside Iceshard Manor, assessing the strength of the Iceshards' forces. We know the brothers have seized control of the kromrif through fear and anger. The traitors wield shards of power, and it would be unwise to underestimate the brothers' capabilities. Rejnak, have you made preparations for the King?'\nRejnak Coldspear shouts 'The priests await his arrival at the temple. When Yetarr and Kyenka receive word that the Iceshards have been dealt with, and that the streets are safe, they will accompany the King to the temple.'\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'A pilgrimage alone will not break the crystal axe's hold upon the King. We may need Klaggan and Vorken's knowledge to release the King. We should not kill them before we have gotten answers.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'I blame no one here if hatred guides a blade that cuts too deep. Whether or not the traitors yet draw breath at the end of the day, we will save the King. Let us meet Captain Bvellos. Adventurers, we follow you to Iceshard Manor.'\n\n---\n\n2\\. Make your way to the entrance of Iceshard Manor 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nThis is the building in the southern part of the zone. If you were coming from Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening, hang a left (south) after passing through the second archway.\nYou won't be able to make it all the way as the area will be blocked by walls of ice. Note that there is a death touch aura around this area that will be removed later on. Do not approach or you will receive a Death Touch.\n3\\. Speak with Captain Bvellos 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Bvellos'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'Halt! Do not get closer to the Manor! The Iceshards must have known we were preparing to strike: They have erected a barrier. A chill wind blows from the ice walls and penetrates my bones. The magic of the crystals must be at work.'\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'You have tested your blade against this barrier, no? Do not tell me you cower in fear of a chill breeze!'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'Do you think half my blade was swallowed by a walrus? Of course I challenged the barrier! We will need more than steel to destroy it.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Sheathe your words, both of you! Bvellos, you have known of this obstacle longer than we. What do you suggest we do?'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'Lean upon Wevek Redforge. He has admitted to crafting the weapons that plague the city. He is fortunate I have not yet claimed his head, and in this matter he may redeem himself.'\n\n---\n\n4\\. Speak with Wevek Redforge 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nIf you were coming from Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening, hang a right (north) after passing through the second archway. Wevek is in one of these buildings. After hailing him you will have about a minute before Drjek enters the room and attacks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Wevek Redforge'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'Have you come to kill me? If you don't do it, Drjek will. The first time I touched those horrible crystals, my fate was written. I have sacrificed Kael to appease my cowardice. My head is yours to take. Do so swiftly that I might die a death befitting a warrior of Zek.'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'Do not think I am reluctant to kill you, Wevek, but your head must remain upon your shoulders for now. What do you know of the barrier that protects Iceshard Manor?'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'I know that Drjek is coming to kill me. Klaggan and Vorken have no need of me now, for it was I who created the barrier.'\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'You traitorous bastard, I have heard enough of your mewling excuses and self-pity!'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Stay your blade, Fjokar! Let him speak.'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'I crafted five crystals that generate the cold wind that blows from the barrier. And the walls themselves I wove with filaments of the crystal, giving them strength to withstand ordinary weapons. You will never enter the Manor. I have doomed the city...'\nRejnak Coldspear shouts 'Is there nothing you can do? Surely the one who created such a thing would know how to dismantle it!'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'The five generator crystals are weaker than the barrier, but they are guarded by the Iceshards' loyalists. If you were able to bring me pieces of these crystals, I might be able to forge a weapon strong enough to break through the barrier. But not if Drjek claims my head -- and I hear footsteps at the door!'\nDrjek shouts 'Wevek, you have interfered with the Iceshards' plans for the last time! With your death, no one will be able to remove the barrier. I told you I would kill you, and I hold to my word!'\n5\\. Kill Drjek 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ Drjek is coming to prevent Wevek Redforge from revealing the secret of the barrier. Kill Drjek before he can silence Wevek.\nDrjek doesn't appear to be any more difficult than a standard trash mob.\nDrjek has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\n6\\. Speak with Wevek Redforge 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wevek Redforge'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'Go and bring me the pieces of crystal. I will forge your weapon on one condition: You will kill me when I have finished. A coward such as I does not deserve to live.'\n\n---\n\n7\\. Destroy the crystal shards boosting the power of the barrier in front of Iceshard Manor 0/5 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Crystal locations:_\n\\- on a platform next to the Wakening Land zone-in (far western part of the zone)\n\\- inside the small building due west of the bank (center of the zone)\n\\- inside one of the buildings northwest of the bank (center of the zone)\n\\- outside one of the vendor buildings in the same area as Wevek's building\n\\- in one of the archways leading in from Zeixshi-Kar's Awakening (east part of the zone)\nNote: Each crystal is guarded by two crystal guards [npc=42591] that are leashed to it. These giants cast a 2-tick damage shield on themselves:\nCrystal Defender: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Damage Shield by 500\n2: Increase Chance to Reflect Spell by 10%\nThe crystals are belly-casters. Once they reach 40%, they spawn \"a shard seeker\" which attacks (the shade is a simple mob for its level).\nPick up the Crystal Remains [item=106593] (on the ground in place of the crystal corpses). Take them to Wevek and hail him to receive a Barrier Breaker [item=106613] (Temporary).\n8\\. Deliver pieces of the destroyed shards to Wevek Redforge 0/5 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n9\\. Speak with Wevek Redforge 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, Wevek Redforge'\nWevek Redforge shouts 'It is finished: Take this axe and undo the damage I have done to the city. May the axe's edge first taste the nape of my neck. May my blood be the first offering of payment due for all of our traitorous actions.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Adventurers, you have proven yourselves noble and wise. I leave unto you the fate of this traitor. '\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'You would leave this matter to them? Your actions seem foolish, but as you are a noble, I defer to your authority rather than your intellect. Come, all, we should not tarry.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'The word has been spread; the kromzek have assembled. Today Iceshard Manor shall fall. Adventurers, destroy the barrier!'\n\n---\n\n10\\. Use the weapon crafted by Wevek Redforge to weaken and destroy the barriers 0/3 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nFrom a distance (or you'll be death touched), target the Iceshard Manor walls of ice and right-click the Barrier Breaker. Do this for all three walls. You'll get an emote, and you can then approach the walls and attack them to destroy them.\nFlame leaps from your crystal axe and destroys the regenerative power of the ice wall.\nWeakening the ice wall with the power of the axe destroys the magic defending Iceshard Manor.\nAs the barrier crumbles, the kromzek rush into Iceshard Manor, eager to kill the traitors within.\nNote: once the 3 ice walls have been destroyed, you may kill Wevek Redforge and loot the Kromrif Locksmith Tools [item=109181] for the quest A Ticket to the Show [quest=6193]. Killing Wevek also grants the achievement A Just Sentence [quest=6546].\n\n---\n\n11\\. Penetrate Iceshard Manor and find Klaggan and Vorken 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n12\\. Speak with Bjoskhua Blackfist 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ The brothers are not here. Speak with Bjoskhua Blackfist and find out where they went.\nNote: About 60 seconds after the hail, all three will attack.\nYou say, 'Hail, Bjoskhua Blackfist'\nBjoskhua Blackfist shouts 'You seek the Iceshards? They are not here. The cowards have left us, their servants, to atone for the crimes they committed. The punishment dealt to the loyal is often worse than that dealt to the leaders they follow. But what could we have done? Does not a servant, if he wishes to live, respond to his master's call?'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'And what of King Tormax? Is he not the master of your masters? Were you deaf when he called?'\nClrakk Blackfist shouts 'Do you call a madman your master? He whom you call king declared war upon the kromrif. I will never call master one who orders my death!'\nRejnak Coldspear shouts 'And who brought this madness upon the King? Your masters, the ones who have left you to die at our hands. Did you not know the plans they held? Do you three not manage the affairs of this manor? Your lies of ignorance will make poor shields against our blades!'\nNojas Blackfist shouts 'We claim only the right to defend our lives. How many years have the kromrif been relegated to the gutters of this city? The kromzek reign in Dragondeath Keep and curry favor with Rallos Zek in the temple. The kromrif rot in Iceshard Manor, their power dwindling, waiting in fear for the day they know will come: the day the kromzek storm the Manor, as you have done, and demand our heads!'\nBjoskhua Blackfist shouts 'What could the Iceshards have done? Cowardly though they may be, they knew this day would arrive. The crystals merely gave us a chance at victory -- and now you are about to snatch that from us, along with our lives. We will not surrender to you. We will not kneel before a mad king who treats his subjects with contempt!'\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'If you will not prostrate yourselves before the authority of the King, then your corpses will do so in your stead!'\nFrom here, they attack.\n13\\. Defeat the three Blackfist brothers 0/3 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ The Blackfist brothers will not give up the location of the Iceshards. Kill them.\nClrakk Blackfist [npc=42580] is stunnable, but not mezzable or snareable. He casts \"Lifedraw Blade\" (adds a lifetap proc to his hits):\nLifedraw Blade: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Lifetap from Weapon Damage\nBjoskhua Blackfist [npc=42579] is mezzable, but not stunnable or snareable. He casts \"Violent Detonation\":\nViolent Detonation: Targeted AE 30', Fire (-960)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 45000\nNojas Blackfist [npc=42581] is snareable, but not mezzable or stunnable. He casts \"Gripping Hold\":\nGripping Hold: Targeted AE 30', Magic (-960)\n1: Decrease Movement by 20000%\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 10 per tick\n3: Increase Curse Counter by 30\nUpon the death of the last Blackfist:\nNoble Helssen shouts 'The manor has been cleansed, but still the Iceshards live. By now the King must be waiting outside the temple entrance. Go to him and speak with Yetarr. Begin the ceremony without me. I must search for the Iceshards. If they remain within Kael, they shall not live long.'\nThe task locks.\n\n---\n\n14\\. Speak to Yetarr in front of the temple 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Task Window Says:_ The king is being led to the temple grounds, where a ritual will take place. Go there and speak to Yetarr.\nYetarr is located in the northern part of the zone, near the Arena, at /way +1457,+1267.\nNote: The Iceshard brothers attack a little over two minutes following Yetarr's hail.\nYou say, 'Hail, Yetarr'\nYetarr shouts 'You did not find the Iceshards? Then we must hurry. Already I fear for the safety of Kael as the King's mind fades, but with Klaggan and Vorken alive, we are all in even greater danger.'\nKing Tormax grips his axe tightly and growls. 'Why do you bring me under sky, under danger? You fools, do you wish to kill your King? Do you wish to kill us all? The dragon looks down upon us! Can you not see it above? Can you not hear its screeches and feel its hot breath?'\nKyenka shouts 'Semkak, Gkrean, begin the ceremony. May your words find favor with Rallos Zek.'\nSemkak Prophet of Vallon shouts 'Rallos Zek, mightiest Warlord, hear our words! Grant King Tormax his mind that he may wield his blade in your name and slay your enemies! With clear thought he will bring death to the coldain and all inferior creatures detestable to you!'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Yetarr, Kyenka, they are here! The Iceshards!'\nSemkak Prophet of Vallon shouts '...and walk upon this land with death in hand, cutting to pieces the weak and unworthy...'\nVorken Iceshard shouts 'Prayer is for the weak and unworthy! Those who have power wield it; they do not petition for it from others!'\nCaptain Bvellos shouts 'Blades ready! Kill the traitors!'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Stay your swords! Do you not see what they carry?'\na crystal of fear begins to vibrate. King Tormax starts shaking, his axe moving synchronously with the crystal's vibration frequency. His lips curl into a snarl, and saliva drips from his mouth.\nKlaggan Iceshard shouts 'Drop your weapons and back away, or King Tormax himself will sever your heads!'\nVorken Iceshard shouts 'Tormax is now ours to command. We are his masters, as it should have been long ago! YOU are now the traitors!'\nWenglawks Kkeak bellows with laughter. 'Look at you, Bvellos, shocked and afraid, wondering if and when King Tormax will take your head! Now you must know what I have felt all these years!'\nWenglawks Kkeak shouts 'He who bows to one man finds his head on the block when his master loses power. But if you bow only to yourself, it does not matter who rises or falls. Your allegiance remains with yourself, and you make allies with whoever keeps you alive. Fanatic loyalty is a trait shared by those who rest in an early grave!'\nWenglawks Kkeak shouts 'Coldain, dragons, giants -- it does not matter. In the end the highest loyalty is bought with coin. Do you think any of us would be where we are if my mercantile savvy had not purchased this crystal from the foolish dragon in Eastern Wastes?'\nWenglawks Kkeak shouts 'My coin and my wits have outlasted you all! And now my newest business partners will give to me the respect and rewards King Tormax should have so many years ago!'\nVorken Iceshard shouts 'Yes, Wenglawks, we will give the reward you deserve! King Tormax, kill this coward! He has betrayed you to the dragons and coldain!'\nKing Tormax roars with rage and lifts his axe as Wenglawks cowers behind the pulsing crystal.\nWenglawks Kkeak shouts 'Klaggan, this is not part of our deal! After all I have given you!'\nKlaggan Iceshard shouts 'What have you given to us? All you have done you did for yourself! Had we been the ones reigning within Dragondeath Keep, you would have bent the crystal against us! The only thing more insidious than the disloyal is one who feigns loyalty! Tormax, kill him!'\nWenglawks Kkeak screams as King Tormax's axe rips through his body. As Tormax swings, the axe cleaves through Wenglawks and strikes the crystal behind which the traitor was hiding. As the crystal begins to sputter, the King staggers back.\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Now, adventurers, draw your weapons! Attack the traitors while King Tormax is stunned!'\n15\\. Defeat the Iceshard brothers 0/2 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nThe brothers auto-aggro (summon from 100% health). Vorken casts Heartstab while Klaggan casts Circle of Steel:\nHeartstab: Single Target, Magic (-960)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 65000\nCircle of Steel: PB AE 150', Magic (-960)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 55000\nUpon their deaths:\nCaptain Bvellos spits on Wenglawks' body. 'A proper reward for traitors!'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'I welcome their deaths as you do, but now we cannot question them about the King's mind.'\nGkrean Prophet of Tallon shouts 'King Tormax, are you well?'\nKing Tormax shakes violently, gripping his axe. He roars to the sky, 'Yelinak, Dane, I see you! Come, fight me! Fight me and die like true warriors!'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'The King will not heed you, Gkrean. The crystal still controls his mind. Adventurers, something must be done before the King loses the last shred of his sanity.'\nFjokar Frozenshard shouts 'We should lead the King back to the Keep. Let us not allow him to be shamed like this in the open.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'No, do not touch him. He will rip you apart. Adventurers, we again need your [help].'\n\n---\n\n16\\. Accept your reward 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou have killed Klaggan and Vorken Iceshard, but the crystal shard of fear still controls King Tormax. A strong force must be gathered to protect the city from King Tormax and bring him back to sanity.\n_Rewards:_\n337 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task) from a chest - Traitors Among Us [npc=42446]:_\nAxe of Splitting Glaciers\nClairvoyant Orb\nFjeka's Fang\nSemkak's Meditative Cincture\nShield of Greatness\nSlagheart's Tail\nSword of the Lone Tarot\nVeil of Anonymity\nVelium Staff of Obliteration\nYetarr's Stonewall Cloak\nMinor Dreadmote\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote",
    },
