      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kael Drakkel, The King's Madness [zone=869]\n**Who:**\n- Noble Helssen [npc=41307]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nDragon Death Keep\n**Related Zones:**\n- Kael Drakkel: The Madness of King Tormax [zone=887]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Dain Frostreaver IV [npc=42610]\n- King Tormax [npc=42602]\n- Lord Yelinak [npc=42611]\n- Noble Helssen [npc=42608]\n- a coldain figment [npc=42609]\n- a crystal of fear [npc=42607]\n- an ornate chest - The Madness of King Tormax [npc=42100]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Kael #1: Deliver Us Unto Evil [quest=6059]\n- Kael #2: Them Bones [quest=6060]\n- Kael #3: A Cure for Madness [quest=6061]\n- Raid Expedition: The Madness of King Tormax [quest=6064]\n- Traitors Among Us [quest=6062]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 21:25:31 2012\nModified: Wed Sep 25 06:34:28 2024 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Note: This is the group mission for \"The Madness of King Tormax\". For the raid, see this quest entry [quest=6064].**\n_This is a group mission that begins with Noble Helssen ( map) in Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness. He is located en route to the throne room of Kael Drakkel (southern part of the zone)._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed \"Deliver Us Unto Evil\"\n\\- Completed \"Them Bones\"\n\\- Completed \"A Cure for Madness\"\n\\- Completed \"Traitors Among Us\" (mission)\n\\- Must have positive faction with Dragon Death Keep (kill frost giants and/or apparitions to increase it)\nYou say, 'Hail, Noble Helssen'\nNoble Helssen says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, you have done well removing the tainted [weapons] from the city and defeating the Iceshards, but now the King's life is in danger. He is under the influence of the crystal, and if he cannot be saved, then Kael will be enveloped in his madness. If you can muster a [large] force, we can divest the King of the crystal's power. If you can only field a [small] group, still we must try!'\nYou say, 'I have a small group'\nNoble Helssen says 'Good. Outside the temple the King still strides about, raving and waving his accursed axe, bellowing epithets at his visions of Dain Frostreaver IV and Lord Yelinak. We must [confront] him now.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Madness of King Tormax'.\nThe giants of Kael require your help to destroy the fear shard that is luring King Tormax into madness.\nYou say, 'Let's confront him'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Kael Drakkel Mission.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Noble Helssen 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, Noble Helssen'\nNoble Helssen says 'We have failed to wake King Tormax from his trance of rage. Every second he grows more agitated, such that we cannot approach him. He defends the crystal, brandishing his axe at anyone who dares glance at the malevolent thing. We have no choice: We must [destroy] the crystal! If you have not the heart to face such trials, [leave] now!'\nYou say, 'Destroy?'\nNoble Helssen says 'Whatever the King may do, or whatever strange apparitions may confront us, we must destroy the crystal. We will fight the King if there is no other option, but we cannot let him fall in battle. Are you [ready]?'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nNoble Helssen says 'Go, adventurers, free the King from his madness!'\n_King Tormax attacks. He hits for a max ~11,000; does not summon; casts \"Banishment of Fears\" every 30 seconds; and casts \"Axe Swipe\" every 40 seconds:_\nBanishment of Fears: PB AE 100', Magic (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 25000\nAxe Swipe: Directional 100', Magic (-940)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 35000\n_Tormax can be rooted off to the side while you DPS the crystal and progress the task._\n\n---\n\nDamage the fear shard controlling King Tormax 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_DPS the fear shard to 75%. This triggers the spawn of three Coldain mobs that attack._\nDefeat coldain figments 0/3 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_These hit for a max ~10,800 and are stunnable, rootable, and snareable. They do not cast any spells._\n_NOTE: While the figments are alive, the crystal has a very small aura around it that pushes you away if you get too close:_\nCrystal Gravitation: Single Target, Unresistable (0)\n1: Slow Push (400)\n_(This is also in effect while Dain and Yelinak are up later in the task.)_\n\n---\n\nDamage the fear shard controlling King Tormax 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_DPS the fear shard to 50% to spawn Dain Frostreaver IV, who attacks._\nDain Frostreaver IV's form takes shape, wielding a heavy, armor-breaking axe.\nDefeat Dain Frostreaver IV 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_He hits for a max ~14,800 and casts \"Dain's Skull Cracker\" every 30 seconds throughout the fight:_\nDain's Skull Cracker: Single Target, Magic (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 32000\n2: Stun (1.00 sec)\n_A ways into the fight (50%?), he adds \"Armored Roll\" to his arsenal (cast every 25 seconds):_\nArmored Roll: PB AE 70', Unresistable (0)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 40000\n\n---\n\nDamage the fear shard controlling King Tormax 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_DPS the fear shard to 25% to spawn Lord Yelinak, who attacks._\nLord Yelinak is manifested from King Tormax's fears!\nDefeat Lord Yelinak 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_NOTE: The task locks upon Yelinak's death._\n_Lord Yelinak hits for a max ~16,000 and casts \"Tail Thunder\" (rear AE), \"Chilling Breath\" (frontal AE), and \"Wing Gust\" (PBAE). Each of these is preceded by an emote 10 seconds in advance of its cast:_\n**Tail Thunder**\n_Warning:_ Lord Yelinak's tail starts to twitch.\n_Seen as it's cast:_ Lord Yelinak thunders his tail against the ground.\nTail Thunder: Directional 70', Magic (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 22000\n2: Stun (2.00 sec)\n**Chilling Breath**\n_Warning:_ Lord Yelinak gathers frost in his throat.\n_Seen as it's cast:_ Lord Yelinak exhales frost.\nChilling Breath: Directional 200', Cold (-950)\n1: Decrease Spell Haste by 15%\n2: Limit: Spell Type (Detrimental only)\n3: Decrease Attack Speed by 25%\n4: Decrease Hitpoints by 25000 per tick\n5: Increase Curse Counter by 50\n**Wing Gust**\n_Warning:_ Lord Yelinak begins to flap his wings.\n_Seen as it's cast:_ Lord Yelinak churns the air with his wings.\nWing Gust: PB AE 100', Cold (-950)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 20000\n\n---\n\nDestroy the fear shard controlling King Tormax 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\n_Destroy the fear shard._\na crystal of fear has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\n\n---\n\nSpeak to King Tormax 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou say, 'Hail, King Tormax'\nKing Tormax looks at the temple grounds. His retainers watch his face and keep their hands upon their weapons. Slowly the King's faculties return. 'Against whom have I fought? Blood seeps from wounds I knew not that I had, and my hand is numb as though I have wielded steel against steel.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'Forgive us your wounds, my King, for your mind was not your own. The brothers of Iceshard wielded a crystal of immense power against you -- against all the citizens of Kael. The brothers now lie in their own blood. May their memory be purged from our minds and records. But though we cut them down, we could not sever the crystal's hold upon you without force.'\nYetarr shouts 'My King, you should retire to the Keep. Allow your wounds and your mind to mend.'\nKing Tormax raises his hand and silences his retainer. 'My mind has remained long enough in idleness. Searching my memory is like peering through a thick fog: I see only flashes of steel and the faces of Dain Frostreaver and Lord Yelinak peering at me, mocking me. What has become of the city in my absence?\nNoble Helssen shouts 'There is much to recount. Many of our people are dead, and it shall be no easy task repairing the trust between the kromrif and kromzek. With your return, though, there is hope the city will not fall to fear and civil war. At your command, my King, we shall enter the Keep and begin immediately to repair the destruction wrought by the Iceshards.'\nKing Tormax looks to Noble Helssen and creases his brow. 'Your words sting more than your steel. My wounds do not compare to those inflicted upon Kael Drakkel. We shall return to the Keep, but I shall take no aid until I have given it to the city.'\nNoble Helssen shouts 'As you command, so shall it be done!' Addressing the adventurers before him, Noble Helssen continues, 'Adventurers, you have proven your worth. You have saved King Tormax and the entire city. I hold you as warriors of great strength and honored friends of Kael Drakkel. When you [leave] here, do so knowing that we are indebted to you.'\n\n---\n\nOpen the chest for your reward 0/1 (Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness)\nYou have destroyed the fear crystal, freeing King Tormax from his haze of madness.\n_Rewards:_\n225 platinum\nExperience\n_Possible Chest Loot [npc=42100] (1 Item + 1 Dreadmote per task):_\nBow of Nature's Caress\nFey Swarm Shawl\nIceflame Band\nInscrutable Talisman\nIre of Reivaj\nPakjol's Appetite for Destruction\nShaman Goliath's Spaulders\nStormcaller's Crystallized Lightning\nVisage of the Prophet\nMinor Dreadmote\nLesser Dreadmote\nMedian Dreadmote\nGreater Dreadmote",
    },
