      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kael Drakkel, The King's Madness [zone=869]\n**Who:**\n- Welverd Steelbairn [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Apparition Flesh [item=106611]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a giant soul eater [npc=42104]\n- a soul scavenger [npc=42105]\n**Era:** | !Rain of Fear\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 28 21:39:06 2012\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Rain of Fear Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task begins with Welverd Steelbairn ( map) in Kael Drakkel: The King's Madness. He's located at 100, 1215, -135. If coming from the Eastern Wastes, pass through the first archway, keep going, pass through the second archway, and hang an immediate right (north). He is outside one of the buildings in this area._\nYou say, 'Hail, Welverd Steelbairn'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'Do you smell that? The miasma begins to waft through Kael, rising from the corpses that lie unburied. Were it not for the preservative qualities of ice, we would all be choking on the stench of rotting flesh by now. But it is [difficult] to approach the bodies of our fallen brethren in order to bury them.'\nYou say, 'Difficult?'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'It is not only because of their repellent smell. There seems to be a kind of darkness clinging to the bodies, some feeling that penetrates whoever draws near. I think it must have some relation to the strange [apparitions] that have arrived in Kael.'\nYou say, 'Apparitions?'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'I struck one down the other day -- one of those twisted dogs. I did not want the meat to go to waste, so I took its body home and cooked it. Even though the meat was burnt, it still tasted raw. Leaving my home later in the evening, I walked near a kromrif's corpse. Crawling around the body were fat, shadowy [worms].'\nYou say, 'What worms?'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'I had never seen anything like those worms, and I thought I was imagining things. On my way home, I did not see the worms there. The next morning, I ate more of the meat, and I walked the path once more. The corpse still lay on the ground, and the worms had returned. I hid behind a snowdrift and watched as they slowly [disappeared] from my sight, seeming to melt into the snow.'\nYou say, 'Disappeared?'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'It must be the meat. It gave me a glimpse into a dark world unknown to giants. The discomfort I felt before around the corpses must come from these shadowy worms. If I could somehow banish them from Kael, we could retrieve our dead and give them proper burial. Would you be willing to [deal] with these worms for me? I do not have the heart to face them, as difficult as it is for me to admit.'\nYou say, 'I will deal with them'\nWelverd Steelbairn says 'Thank you. Here is some of the meat I saved from the dead apparition. If you eat it, you will surely see the worms. If you run out of meat, kill and eat more apparitions.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bring Out Your Dead'.\n_You receive \"Apparition Flesh\"._\nThe dead in Kael lie unburied, but Welverd Steelbairn wants to change this. To allow the giants to properly care for the deceased, you must kill the shadow worms that have been feeding upon the dead giants.\nThe shadow worms can be found near corpses of giants. In order to see and fight the shadow worms without causing grave harm to yourself, you must consume the flesh of apparitions.\n\n---\n\nReceive a piece of Apparition Flesh from Welverd Steelbairn 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n_This is an auto-update._\nKill 6 soul scavengers 0/6 (Kael Drakkel)\nKill 2 giant soul eaters 0/2 (Kael Drakkel)\n_With the Apparition Flesh self-buff on you (4-minute duration), engage and kill soul scavengers and soul eaters around the corpses of giants. You need the buff to do this, or you will be DT'd._\n_You can kill other apparitions to pick up more flesh clicks as you need them._\nReturn to Welverd Steelbairn 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n(Optional) Kill apparitions of dragons, coldain, and other creatures to gain more flesh pieces 0/20 (Kael Drakkel)\n_Rewards:_\n187 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience",
    },
