      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kael Drakkel [ToV]\n**Who:**\n- Derakor the Vindicator - ToV [ _Quest_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 110\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Related Creatures:**\n- an aggressive corpse - ToV [npc=55202]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Citizens Revolting [quest=9758]\n- Heroes Must Die (Again) [quest=9771]\n- Partisan of Kael Drakkel (10 Points) [quest=9804]\n- Put Soldiers to Rest [quest=9770]\n**Era:** | !Torment of Velious\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 3 22:12:22 2019\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Torment of Velious Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n**Prerequisite Quest(s):** Citizens Revolting > Put Soldiers to Rest > Heroes Must Die (Again)\nThis is the first Group task given by Derakor the Vindicator. You can find him at /way -323, -7, -155 on the far north side of the zone.\nDerakor the Vindicator is in charge of defending King Tormax against the restless dead. Because of this obligation, he cannot leave his post but he would like to assist any survivors that are holding out in Kael. He has asked you to follow up on the rumors about giants holding out in the bank and merchant areas.\nYou say, 'Hail, Derakor the Vindicator'\nDerakor the Vindicator says, 'Hello, tiny creature. You look like any of your kind, I suppose. Perhaps we have met before, I do not know. No matter, I am pleased that you have found your way here through these,' he waves his hand at the restless corpses banging on the barrier or wandering the grounds outside, 'unfortunate people. I will personally remove the head of the Coldain or dragon or whatever creature has caused this. Until that time I must stand guard here to protect those of us that [remain].'\nYou say, 'remain'\nDerakor the Vindicator says, 'Not many of us have survived. Not only do we face the greatest warriors ever born, but they are already dead. No enemy could be more dangerous. We few have been able to survive here, and I can only hope that others have found defensible locations. Our situation is ultimately untenable. Every one that falls becomes an enemy. We have been forced to burn our dead. It is a horrible insult to such great warriors, but we have no other option if we are to survive. If the number of restless dead is not [reduced], we will all join their ranks.'\nYou say, 'reduced'\nDerakor the Vindicator says, 'We really could use your assistance in that effort. We are a wise people and honor our dead with proper ritual and reverence. Anyone disrupting the bodies of our dead is treated harshly. Our people do not cause harm to those that have battled their last before us. Even now we hesitate to harm them, and that hesitation has cost us several lives. I cannot order my men out to destroy their friends and heroes. I would be grateful if you could apply your [skills] to reducing the horde.'\nYou say, 'skills'\nDerakor the Vindicator says, 'You have served us well, little one. I have another task for you. While I would approve if you kept helping with the restless dead, I want to know if others have survived. If so, we must let them know that the king still rules Kael.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Find the Survivors'.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Contact any survivors in or near the merchant area, if they are alive 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\nYou will need to talk to Kellek Fellhammer located at /way -2333, -96, -282. He is standing next to Svekk Fangbinder which can be found on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kellek Felhammer'\nKellek Felhammer says, 'What? The Vindicator sent you? It is good to hear that the king still lives. We here have managed to drive those dead things away, but they keep coming back. Some of them are far more aggressive than the others. Please deal with any of the more aggressive dead if you can.'\nYour task 'Find the Survivors' has been updated.\n2\\. Contact any survivors in or near the bank, if they are alive 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\nOne group member goes to hail Yetarr [npc=55339] in the merchant area (most southeast room) while other members go the bank and hail either Svekk Fangbinder [npc=55299] or Kellek Felhammer [npc=55240].\nKellek Felhammer says, 'What? The Vindicator sent you? It is good to hear that the king still lives. We here have managed to drive those dead things away, but they keep coming back. Some of them are far more aggressive than the others. Please deal with any of the more aggressive dead if you can.'\nYour task 'Find the Survivors' has been updated.\nYou say, 'Hail, Yetarr'\nYetarr says, 'Ah, adventurers. So, you have spoken with Derakor and you say that the king lives. I am unsurprised. The Vindicator and the elite guards should be able to stand firm against these monstrosities. It has been a challenge for us. After all, one of the monsters that we had to put down was a cousin of mine. If you could deal with any of the more aggressive monsters, we would feel a lot safer. And give the king my regards.'\nYour task 'Find the Survivors' has been updated.\n3\\. Clear the aggressive undead from near their hiding place 0/8 (Kael Drakkel)\nApparently there are some more aggressive restless dead that have been attracted to the living. These are the most dangerous to the living giants. They would like you to deal with some of them.\nKill 8 aggressive corpses near the bank where Kellek Felhammer and Svekk Fangbinder are. The live giants will attack you too so watch out for them.\n4\\. Tell Derakor the Vindicator what you have learned 0/1 Kael Drakkel\nDerakor the Vindicator says, 'It is good to hear that some still live. Some day we will make whoever was responsible for this pay!'\nYour task 'Find the Survivors' has been updated.\n_Derakor was pleased that you could help his people._\n_\n---\n_\n_Reward(s):_\n_212 platinum 5 gold_\n_You gain experience!_\n**Submitted by:** Cylius & Laurana",
