in my blood! I'll be one of them in no time. Someone has to go find Frost and [ **put him down**]. I hear that if you kill the one that bit you it will stop you from turning.'\nYou say, 'put him down'\nSvekk Fangbinder says, 'I mean, he's already dead, right? And I don't want to turn into one of those things! Go find him and mash his head in!'\nSvell is extremely concerned with a bite he got from his undead once-pet wolf called Frost. He is desperate that you find a way to cure him before he turns into an undead.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Kill Svekk's restless pet dire wolf Frost 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n> **Task Window Text:** Svekk is convinced that if you kill the dog that bit him, his own direwolf called Frost, this will prevent him from turning into one of the restless dead.\nKill Frost. He can spawn in multiple places, including as a 'companion' wolf to various giants in the zone.\n2\\. Find and kill the sorcerer that killed Frost 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n> **Task Window Text:** Find and kill the restless dead that killed the direwolf called Frost.\nKill a Kromzek sorcerer located in the throne room at -2411, 217, -229.\n3\\. Tell Svekk that you killed Frost and the sorcerer that killed the wolf 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n> **Task Window Text:** Svell is truly panicked now. He wants you to shave some silver into a flask of water, then find a priest of Zek to bless it so that he can drink it. He thinks holy water or silver will cure him, so he wants both at once.\nYou say, 'Hail, Svekk Fangbinder'\nSvekk Fangbinder says, 'You did? Well, I don't feel any better. What do I do now? Maybe the myths can help me. I remember that my mum told me that silver worked against these sorts of things. Or maybe it was holy water? I know, let's do both!' Svekk pulls a silver coin and a bottle of water from a pouch. Using his skinning knife, he shaves some silver from the coin into the bottle. 'Can you get this blessed for me? Please!'\nYour task 'Wolf Bites Giant' has been updated.\nYou have been given: Silver Infused Bottle of Water\n4\\. Find a priest of Zek to bless the tincture 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n> **Task Window Text:** Find a priest of Zek to bless the silver water. you probably want a living priest.\nGive the Silver Infused Bottle of Water to a priest of Tallon/Vallon Zek and receive a Blessed Tincture of Silver. There is a 'live' Priest in the South Eastern most room that is not KOS. You can do the hand in and there is no need to fight or kill him.\nYou offered 1 Silver Infused Bottle of Water to a priest of Vallon Zek.\nA priest of Vallon Zek looks at you with some suspicion, 'We have heard that you are assisting us. I guess I can bless this, though I can't see what you would want it for.' The priest chants in a sonorous voice for a few moments. As he does so the water turns slightly red. When the chanting is done, he hands the bottle back to you without further comment.\nYou complete the trade with a priest of Vallon Zek.\nYour task 'Wolf Bites Giant' has been updated.\nYou have been given: Blessed Tincture of Silver\n5\\. Give the tincture of silver to Svekk 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\nYou offered 1 Blessed Tincture of Silver to Svekk Fangbinder.\nSvekk Fangbinder takes the flask, hands shaking, and hurriedly tries to drink its contents. He spills much of it in his haste.\nYou complete the trade with Svekk Fangbinder.\nYour task 'Wolf Bites Giant' has been updated.\n6\\. See if Svekk thinks he is cured 0/1 (Kael Drakkel)\n> **Task Window Text:** Ask Svekk if he thinks he is cured yet.\nYou say, 'Hail, Svekk Fangbinder'\nSvekk Fangbinder says, 'Well, I still feel ill. Any moment now I'll turn into a monster! You must...'\nSvekk Fangbinder says, 'Well, I still feel ill. Any moment now I'll turn into a monster! You must...'\nYour task 'Wolf Bites Giant' has been updated.\nSvekk Fangbinder says, 'Well, I still feel ill. Any moment now I'll turn into a monster! You must...'\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Wolf Bites Giant': 0d:0h:30m remaining.\nYou receive 425 platinum .\nYou have gained 1 mercenary ability point(s)!\nYou have gained 23 ability point(s)!\nYou gain experience!\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n425 platinum\nExperience\n1 Merc AA Point (at level 120)\n23 AA Points (at level 120)\n**Submitted by:** Larth",
